      "options": {},
      "values": {
        "text": {
          "Text": "Render 3D's picture is an ordinary picture, so any video node can take it: a turning ring of balls and a torus is folded by a Kaleidoscope and tinted by a Color Shift. Try the Kaleidoscope's Segments and Zoom, or cable Render 3D straight into the Output to see what is being folded. A blur after a render is costly \u2014 it marches the scene again for every tap."
        }
      },
